{"title":"2017 USAJMO Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2(No_Bash)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2(No Bash)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_Without_the_nasty_computations\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 Without the nasty computations</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/4/1e4bb5c0261c8d726157108cdd95cf6eb7bb6d46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$*$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\" />) Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be an equilateral triangle and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be a point on its circumcircle. Let lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/7/377291318df52e4f013ab2bf28ee82454a9e57da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />; let lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/9/9f988caff51f7fc88ad40d1d25022c52ffd8f976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e657259c0995d2c36d46744bb4aa81471e6575ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />; and let lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/e/30e049532148caaf1c48e37658b548a6255c8d59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Prove that the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e9e8b2c23e0545ef6de81f0ea578173e9ab7a64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DEF$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> is twice that of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Proceed via Barycentrics. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/1/9b160a29ccdc01c6578fb982275cb48a46d88970.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x:y:z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/f/75f3ff1b70b1c724fd7e63526b44fdaf9fbb58d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D = (0 : y : z), E= (x:0:z), F=(x:y:0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"354\" height=\"20\" />. Normalizing, we want to prove <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/4/fb42ea06813b2432381d8a32cb35eae374f49405.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2=\\frac{[DEF]}{[ABC]} = \\left(\\frac{1}{y+z}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{x+z}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{x+y}\\right) \\begin{vmatrix} 0 &amp; y &amp; z \\\\ x &amp; 0 &amp; z \\\\ x &amp; y &amp; 0 \\end{vmatrix}\\]\" width=\"412\" height=\"65\" />\n</p><p>The determinant is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/d/7adf13d3a44946efaba73797146649d9a6636aae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2xyz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"17\" />, but since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is on the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, one of the coordinates is negative. Thus, we should use the positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/3/e63eef7f1c600c9edaec22b48399b30e897ede81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2xyz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" /> in our calculations. To finish, we note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> being equilateral implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/8/958cdcf6feead5c539530ed7e083252684476b7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy+xz+yz=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"138\" height=\"17\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/2/7b287a43efa374ce764dd885cff0d87374852d37.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2(y+z)(x+z)(x+y) = -2xyz \\iff x^2y+x^2z+y^2x+ y^2z+z^2x+z^2y +3xyz = 0\\]\" width=\"599\" height=\"20\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/2/5e279d0e8ecae182251f8cbe5f0b12dd12bd37d1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\iff (x+y+z)(xy+xz+yz) = 0\\]\" width=\"280\" height=\"18\" /> as needed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />  \n</p><p>-sillybone\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2.28No_Bash.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2(No_Bash)\">Solution 2(No Bash)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2(No Bash)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/c/78c3af92031ce82e11f57a21c37bc147a0b11852.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]     size(3inch);     pair A = (0, 3sqrt(3)), B = (-3,0), C = (3,0), P = (0, -sqrt(3)), D = (0, 0), E1 = (6, -3sqrt(3)), F = (-6, -3sqrt(3)), O = (0, sqrt(3));     draw(Circle(O, 2sqrt(3)), black);     draw(A--B--C--cycle);     draw(B--E1--C);     draw(C--F--B);     draw(A--P);     draw(D--E1--F--cycle, dashed);     label(&quot;A&quot;, A, N);     label(&quot;B&quot;, B, W);     label(&quot;C&quot;, C, E);     label(&quot;P&quot;, P, S);     label(&quot;D&quot;, D, NW);     label(&quot;E&quot;, E1, SE);     label(&quot;F&quot;, F, SW); [/asy]\" width=\"362\" height=\"322\" />\n</p><p>Extend <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/3/783d500281f8f46167dff3b071c543d42150e67f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DP$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> to hit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" />. Then note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/3/b03f68386ad8653e9cc02e483b54327f841113b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[DEF]\\cdot\\frac{AK}{DK}\\cdot\\frac{AB}{AF}\\cdot\\frac{AC}{AE}=[ABC].$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"275\" height=\"38\" /> Letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/c/cfcf1f17e779cd997a952354192d3a9f8155b8da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BF=x$\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/7/307f41090521f97a9aecfa9180447d372f6a1639.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PF=y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" />, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/2/d72d2ee44d3b3253fd71b8d0d1642a91627ebd87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x+AB}y=\\frac{y+PC}x=\\frac{AC}{BP}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"214\" height=\"41\" /> Solving and simplifying using LoC on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/c/fac056ce386c7154c5ed723c55b2808cc0357fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BPC$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/e/54e8002c513d7a8b834428248f510c5ee3eb5409.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AB}{AF}=\\frac{PC}{PB+PC}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"143\" height=\"39\" /> Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/6/a2698889742f1d50999c6ae7eb1ba07626bde925.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AC}{AE}=\\frac{PB}{PB+PC}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"147\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>Now we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/6/e066e96a5398db430f403fd1fb1719039dc8a89a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AK}{DK}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"43\" height=\"39\" /> Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/0651050adc7727024f82866caa53fe4434bba66a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AD}{DP}=\\frac{AD}{BD}\\cdot\\frac{BD}{DP}=\\frac{AC}{PB}\\cdot\\frac{AB}{PC}=\\frac{AB^2}{PB\\cdot PC}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"344\" height=\"39\" /> Now let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/4/0c40b86c8eb49107c13e9e4d1cc3dec1383902ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E&#39;=DE\\cap AF$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"121\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/6/a46f9c1c569a6b449fa8496eaa540bd008c24a11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F&#39;=DF\\cap AE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" />. Then by an area/concurrence theorem, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/6/fd67b371567fe16442a8022ab2860a9893acceec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{DK}{AK}+\\frac{DE&#39;}{EE&#39;}+\\frac{DF&#39;}{FF&#39;}=1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"195\" height=\"38\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/9/e19ea6c5bff88335434751c00b22a50e429ca271.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{DK}{AK}+(1-\\frac{DP}{AP}-\\frac{DC}{BC})+(1-\\frac{DP}{AP}-\\frac{BD}{BC})=1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"388\" height=\"37\" /> Thus we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/b/78bd8d6e3e1cfa38daad199be874ef08660c976b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{DK}{AK}=2\\cdot\\frac{DP}{AP}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"120\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>Manipulating these gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/a/46a3563e700d366ec955e72642af72cdd84a033b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AK}{DK}=\\frac{(PB+PC)^2}{2\\cdot PB\\cdot PC}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"169\" height=\"39\" /> Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/3/793872e52d1c59e29fe6088bc009f5de209229aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AK}{DK}\\cdot\\frac{AB}{AF}\\cdot\\frac{AC}{AE}=\\frac12,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"168\" height=\"38\" /> and we are done.\n</p><p>~coco hearts \nEdited by I’maSTAY\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>WLOG, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/a/e5a649aee592a9c37d2f9b5d5239f5e06e533130.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/1/67188172e8565c60236ee67b31b69817525e5ced.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABD] = X, [ACD] = Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"193\" height=\"18\" />, and  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/e/e8ea7bbf89c830a2487b3462d99bac0bda5c929e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAD = \\theta$\" width=\"89\" height=\"13\" />. After some angle chasing, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/0/d8016338027cfb0155d2a2fa03ab9f9f0b4e1902.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BCF \\cong \\angle BEC \\cong \\theta$\" width=\"169\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/a/bba3b91463d315461f8a6b832014757af625fa64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle FBC \\cong \\angle BCE \\cong 120^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"194\" height=\"13\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53f25270bba5a9ce0fa8c57649094c4fc815919.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle FBC$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> ~ <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/3/423d2cdb9f74980709bf26fc4bb3cb0304964a8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BCE$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Lemma 1: If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/5/3f5271dd69d1aad073bbbd6c331ffed42bed5f60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BF = k$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/3/893248129f1b9a5796ea6b3a04c753e2df1d8428.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE = \\frac 1k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"65\" height=\"37\" />.\nThis lemma results directly from the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53f25270bba5a9ce0fa8c57649094c4fc815919.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle FBC$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> ~ <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/3/423d2cdb9f74980709bf26fc4bb3cb0304964a8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BCE$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />;  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/b/ecb86eb5aa22fbe42e32b5ae185a4a010eaaea8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{BF}{BC} = \\frac{BF}{1} = \\frac{BC}{CE} = \\frac{1}{CE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"202\" height=\"38\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/9/a796b2f05118f777aca5f1b8875fdb33873577c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE = \\frac{1}{BF}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"88\" height=\"38\" />. \n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Lemma 2: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/a/4da8119cefdd66281441f34a4fd54e20793a63b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[AEF] = (k+\\frac 1k + 2)(X+Y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"234\" height=\"37\" />.\nWe see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/f/42f8feb2b9cc87c81820cd7ec361e409bffb0d07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[AEF] = (X+Y) \\frac{[AEF]}{[ABC]} = (k+1)(1+\\frac 1k)(X+Y) = (k + \\frac 1k + 2)(X+Y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"589\" height=\"43\" />, as desired. \n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Lemma 3: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/1/8a175147684a1184fed1b5f7508b756ca87e82f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{X}{Y} = k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"54\" height=\"37\" />.\nWe see that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7ca410d8ba19acf42e7035766268b251fd1b267.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac XY = \\frac{\\frac 12 (AB)(AD) \\sin(\\theta)}{\\frac 12 (AC)(AD) \\sin (60^{\\circ} - \\theta)} = \\frac{\\sin(\\theta)}{\\sin (60^{\\circ} - \\theta)}.\\]\" width=\"364\" height=\"47\" />\nHowever, after some angle chasing and by the Law of Sines in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/c/6acd42ef30a6319e5b63f48ae3e8a11120e56f63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BCF$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/b/93bed96acd529cb748854e399e2f08554a47cef7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{k}{\\sin(\\theta)} = \\frac{1}{\\sin(60^{\\circ} - \\theta)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"169\" height=\"42\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/c/dec9f041f9adfa7abf6f9d89e920d005386bac0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = \\frac{\\sin(\\theta)}{\\sin (60^{\\circ} - \\theta)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"130\" height=\"43\" />, which implies the result. \n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>By the area lemma, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/9/8b9202b83f19235597a2ec433027a9d3c9f241b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[BDF] = kX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/3/8b36c4cd5cef4f2f2aa320a239e49bc851425b30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[CDF] = \\frac{Y}{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"95\" height=\"37\" />. \n</p><p>We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/8/768c78270479a996a289b43d0adbc23fd6807f07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[DEF] = [AEF] - [ABC] - [BDF] - [DCE] = Xk + Yk + \\frac Xk + \\frac Yk + 2X + 2Y - X - Y - Xk - \\frac Yk = X + Y + \\frac Xk + yk$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"961\" height=\"37\" />. Thus, it suffices to show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/3/303baa786328d7a4af792e283af97c675592b6c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X + Y + \\frac Xk + Yk = 2X + 2Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"238\" height=\"37\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/4/1a44b3149683121612ca9a0b8719a6acc697292b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac Xk + Yk = X + Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"144\" height=\"37\" />. Rearranging, we find this to be equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/0/0c0f89b2548a07729c8afac4783ff4bb0aded9bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac XY = k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"54\" height=\"37\" />, which is Lemma 3, so the result has been proven.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We will use barycentric coordinates and vectors. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/4/68450e99a2bbe28ae4c9e0ed7e6eced243e7a1e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\vec{X}$\" width=\"15\" height=\"17\" /> be the position vector of a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/f/87fa832bf21ebc48a46289cd7aea73ffcc84c111.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X.$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> The point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/b/31b1e1af4531148cbc079023f68c2b0102c4ee69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, y, z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"61\" height=\"20\" /> in barycentric coordinates denotes the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/7/0976cf8860949e87bd5dcebd335f4acaf54a6245.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\vec{A} + y\\vec{B} + z\\vec{C}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"120\" height=\"21\" /> For all points in the plane of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/4/cd4487f46da167d386b12379776dec9429808e9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABC},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"63\" height=\"17\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/d/d9dfc824b61dd2901d6bfd8a319815024bb4caac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y + z = 1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"110\" height=\"15\" /> It is clear that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/9/5594734f575ba9bb2b41af9aebde75dcddb18834.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = (1, 0, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" />; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/f/4ef78f5ccf5a4501c80d01c6131c71361ef7a553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = (0, 1, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />; and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/6/7a676a3d28b77631927a76b21a18740e3b2a7d91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = (0, 0, 1).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Define the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/0/a30a57f86e196f7080122830429e5bdc4050e379.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P = \\left(x_P, y_P, z_P\\right).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" /> The fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies on the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f828f10cad9235a2c72c34369f5fd4a1179e579.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABC}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/c/73cc1f164ca00841d2852b2248b1cbd16f8ec967.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2_P + y^2_P + z^2_P = 1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"142\" height=\"19\" /> This, along with the condition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/3/bc3ae995d2e413746edd347b50b4e6539c382e01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_P + y_P + z_P = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"137\" height=\"15\" /> inherent to barycentric coordinates, gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/8/2c835d6f940d1a72e3a7781781f235edd38fc96b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_Py_P + y_Pz_P + z_Px_P = 0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"203\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>We can write the equations of the following lines:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/7/4f75a212c771547eb84c7dffb6a74ec2a92b2b74.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[BC: x = 0\\]\" width=\"87\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/6/cd6e2385e56f925844127af60bc6f199b3d6eb18.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[CA: y = 0\\]\" width=\"85\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/d/a3d19b7f8420554e0634e013b14241964faf6fc7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AB: z = 0\\]\" width=\"85\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/2/9f25a6560e0699ee2751e17638e46b426038023f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[PA: \\frac{y}{y_P} = \\frac{z}{z_P}\\]\" width=\"113\" height=\"36\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/6/6066a4b3866d1c71e279207f1e88be51bba26f3c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[PB: \\frac{x}{x_P} = \\frac{z}{z_P}\\]\" width=\"115\" height=\"35\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/a/5cafb243f230ca12ff15248cb3d686144c7e7780.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[PC: \\frac{x}{x_P} = \\frac{y}{y_P}.\\]\" width=\"120\" height=\"36\" />\n</p><p>We can then solve for the points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/8/c18e240b7c7dbc4b2e6da70cd13ba155dc475c0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D, E, F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/3/773a130e401ecda63742c1d2ffa71494e836e7b1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[D = \\left(0, \\frac{y_P}{y_P + z_P}, \\frac{z_P}{y_P + z_P}\\right)\\]\" width=\"218\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/2/252765ae003cb9d62d9550db69b80782f778675c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[E = \\left(\\frac{x_P}{x_P + z_P}, 0, \\frac{z_P}{x_P + z_P}\\right)\\]\" width=\"220\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/9/1f90b942779e6fca401313fb3688f1261fa713c1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[F = \\left(\\frac{x_P}{x_P + y_P}, \\frac{y_P}{x_P + y_P}, 0\\right).\\]\" width=\"231\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>The area of an arbitrary triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/2/0526e1f5ad1412706cf938657f754604e672a671.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XYZ$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> is:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/f/31fd837ab533bbc512f5e61e86da03f032354223.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[XYZ] = \\frac{1}{2}|\\vec{XY}\\times\\vec{XZ}|\\]\" width=\"182\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/7/dc7f5a777b43afc9c97e4904ef735f1dde2ad5b0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[XYZ] = \\frac{1}{2}|(\\vec{X}\\times\\vec{Y}) + (\\vec{Y}\\times\\vec{Z}) + (\\vec{Z}\\times\\vec{X})|.\\]\" width=\"347\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>To calculate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/f/20f784e102336c670a3b80c0d58bd72a53a5f806.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[DEF],$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> we wish to compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/5/765c980062c12c2d52b1a3cb8e97a1a9de972093.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\vec{D}\\times\\vec{E}) + (\\vec{E}\\times\\vec{F}) + (\\vec{F}\\times\\vec{D}).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"245\" height=\"22\" /> After a lot of computation, we obtain the following:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/2/1922493e4e7c3c69b6f8a0154666806520cf5bad.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(\\vec{D}\\times\\vec{E}) + (\\vec{E}\\times\\vec{F}) + (\\vec{F}\\times\\vec{D}) = \\frac{2x_Py_Pz_P}{(x_P + y_P)(y_P + z_P)(z_P + x_P)}[(\\vec{A}\\times\\vec{B}) + (\\vec{B}\\times\\vec{C}) + (\\vec{C}\\times\\vec{A})].\\]\" width=\"671\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Evaluating the denominator,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/e/8eea8cbe65c5b692fd2daa92a24637b12c467e5a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x_P + y_P)(y_P + z_P)(z_P + x_P) = (1 - z_P)(1 - y_P)(1 - x_P)\\]\" width=\"449\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/8/f1861b7cfffa2fdebf789ba68478e3dee149da05.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x_P + y_P)(y_P + z_P)(z_P + x_P) = 1 - (x_P + y_P + z_P) + (x_Py_P + y_Pz_P + z_Px_P) - x_Py_Pz_P.\\]\" width=\"613\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/3/bc3ae995d2e413746edd347b50b4e6539c382e01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_P + y_P + z_P = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"137\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/c/52ca4392455a06599910ed2b89db43b5c22fdc23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_Py_P + y_Pz_P + z_Px_P = 0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"203\" height=\"16\" /> it follows that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/4/5842c9a37361e2470cc8944acadf8d0e4db46c2f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x_P + y_P)(y_P + z_P)(z_P + x_P) = -x_Py_Pz_P.\\]\" width=\"332\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>We thus conclude that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/b/32ba490af26f9597a4d6dfa6f995d5ccf63e800d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(\\vec{D}\\times\\vec{E}) + (\\vec{E}\\times\\vec{F}) + (\\vec{F}\\times\\vec{D}) = -2[(\\vec{A}\\times\\vec{B}) + (\\vec{B}\\times\\vec{C}) + (\\vec{C}\\times\\vec{A})].\\]\" width=\"477\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p>From this, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/2/362413d6390bccc7eb593562e5072efb46f37ba7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[DEF] = 2[ABC],$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" /> and we are done.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/d/10d76c13207b6356c0ebc7833813448e1e89cd04.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]    import cse5;    import graph;    import olympiad;      size(3inch);           pair A = (0, 3sqrt(3)), B = (-3,0), C = (3,0), O = (0, sqrt(3));     pair P = (-1, -sqrt(11)+sqrt(3));     path circle = Circle(O, 2sqrt(3));     pair D = extension(A,P,B,C);     pair E1 = extension(A,C,B,P);     pair F=extension(A,B,C,P);     draw(circle, black);     draw(A--B--C--cycle);     draw(B--E1--C);     draw(C--F--B);     draw(A--P);     draw(D--E1--F--cycle, dashed);     pair G = extension(O,D,F,E1);     draw(O--G,dashed);     label(&quot;A&quot;, A, N);     label(&quot;B&quot;, B, W);     label(&quot;C&quot;, C, E);     label(&quot;P&quot;, P, S);     label(&quot;D&quot;, D, NW);     label(&quot;E&quot;, E1, SE);     label(&quot;F&quot;, F, SW);     dot(&quot;O&quot;, O, SE); [/asy]\" width=\"332\" height=\"362\" /></center>\n<p>We'll use coordinates and shoelace. Let the origin be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/2/d5204a6910d20a4ff2968ad55671e3cfa350e9da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=2$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/7/017ba4ffd3acc4d945e31e0433674af42f2f9a4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BF = 2x$\" width=\"72\" height=\"12\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/f/c4f21b145ebbfd5fb37f1efab735d76f59f7afe7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F=(-x-1,-x\\sqrt{3})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"163\" height=\"21\" />. Using the facts <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/1/2115f4e5a1bf16ca997cb297a271b8fb90eb1c86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{CBP} \\sim  \\triangle{CFB}$\" width=\"142\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/b/2bbe86e37cc136b0e8f8412839d4d8c05dad3f62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{BCP} \\sim  \\triangle{BEC}$\" width=\"143\" height=\"13\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/4/2b432bc602caf7e92249c4428d9feddfcfc8d006.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BF * CE = BC^2$\" width=\"134\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/7/48755fdd41bfab5a44c5aedd96856d195275eb2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE = \\frac{1}{2x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"74\" height=\"37\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/6/f465e1fb9d1ff0f74c8e743b8ee78e6b0889d8dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E = (\\frac{1}{x}+1,-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{x})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"147\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>The slope of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/b/52b3b006e6f9fe1681bd1f340795f789d888318e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FE$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> is \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/c/e0cf01f69ae67429fdf887a8ea72d67e2797ef10.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k = \\frac{-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{x} + x\\sqrt{3}}{2+\\frac{1}{x}+x}\\]\" width=\"128\" height=\"50\" />\nIt is well-known that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/d/afdeac9b6991ae1083a00ca40c3939ff0c173a9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{DFE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> is self-polar, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/b/52b3b006e6f9fe1681bd1f340795f789d888318e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FE$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> is the polar of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, i.e., <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/5/46569d6dd3fa86f698827e8de15b0480e1733d11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> is perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/b/52b3b006e6f9fe1681bd1f340795f789d888318e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FE$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />. Therefore, the slope of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/5/46569d6dd3fa86f698827e8de15b0480e1733d11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/b/10b696634526d26a52b84a6453922838be933c8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{1}{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"30\" height=\"38\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/2/1f2bdd12031756310c622630fb23ff7334426273.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O=(0,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"96\" height=\"41\" />, we get the x-coordinate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/a/28abb4cf135db3c1eede2634d9b6498887f6ae1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_D = \\frac{k}{\\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"73\" height=\"42\" />, i.e., <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/8/538f69e8c7819b895b62f86952c261736804c877.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D = (\\frac{k}{\\sqrt{3}},0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"97\" height=\"42\" />. Using shoelace,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/1/b01ca5704d9ddf13c5b68604b6a1cd0e87eca38a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2[\\triangle{FDE}] = \\frac{k}{\\sqrt{3}}(-x\\sqrt{3})+(-x-1)(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{x})-   (-x\\sqrt{3})(\\frac{1}{x}+1) - (-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{x})\\frac{k}{\\sqrt{3}}\\]\" width=\"553\" height=\"45\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/e/6bede91d195b24a48334ce3b1ace83274d2a4fed.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= 2\\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{3}(\\frac{1}{x}+x) + k(\\frac{1}{x} - x)\\]\" width=\"251\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/b/26bbe95e4a419261a2c1ef8ef4b64e0644bbf70b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= 2\\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{3}(\\frac{2(\\frac{1}{x}+x)+(\\frac{1}{x}+x)^2-(\\frac{1}{x}-x)^2} {2+\\frac{1}{x}+x})\\]\" width=\"357\" height=\"47\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/d/2fd8789e1438afef94543c7906c96412ab05e3f3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= 2\\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{3}(\\frac{2(\\frac{1}{x}+x)+4}{2+\\frac{1}{x}+x})\\]\" width=\"213\" height=\"47\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/3/d93995a8c34549c8c9c1f5dfe6bb0ef401527831.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= 4\\sqrt{3}\\]\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />\nSo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/1/e415e4dda49efce20a92c8fffa925760babfb477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\triangle{FDE}] = 2\\sqrt{3} = 2[\\triangle{ABC}]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"228\" height=\"22\" />. Q.E.D\n</p><p>By Mathdummy.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_Without_the_nasty_computations\">Solution 6 Without the nasty computations</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 Without the nasty computations\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/6/416ad67b8eeb8736970f081542dc5ecdf49ad201.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{APB}=\\angle{FPB}=\\angle{EPC}=\\angle{APC} = 60$\" width=\"336\" height=\"13\" />. We will use a special version of Stewart's theorem for angle bisectors in triangle with an 120 angle to calculate various side lengths. \n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/a/daa40ce94e83ec3f2159adb90185d0b586d0edfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BP = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/c/8cc0988d19ab629932b915d220ce79107b8920fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CP = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" />. Then,\nFrom Law of Cosine, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e334ac44b4012f36257ae093b47f89e2a24568eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC^2 = x^2 + y^2 + xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"159\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>From Ptolemy's theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/3/953bc5ea0632906e16f03fc2228f06f976dc1554.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP BC = x AC + y AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"178\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/b/e5bb445eb951145846112eb4dbea65961b6bf419.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP = x + y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Lemma 1: In Triangle ABC with side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/a/e6a44c255357164501168be83218f4fe943cdd65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A =120^o$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"84\" height=\"13\" />, the length of the angle bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/e/50ed73e1fee8b7aa384198e42e07c7463cdff2e5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d = \\frac{bc}{b+c}\\]\" width=\"73\" height=\"39\" />\nThis can be easily proved with Stewart's and Law of Cosine.\n</p><p>Using Lemma 1, we have \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/0/0e0639a09c7c05f4da3c9848807172495ac7433d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[PD = \\frac{xy}{x+y}\\]\" width=\"98\" height=\"36\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/a/46a4ee572f919142662a1b0aebc76b0795b1e8d1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = \\frac{FP AP}{FP + AP}\\]\" width=\"114\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/c/65c51c9957319fdffd54a82ee1d2b776ee5ca086.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y = \\frac{EP AP}{EP + AP}\\]\" width=\"114\" height=\"39\" />\nPlug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/2/722d3557012477719b90570913d2ced65d84af96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP=x+y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" />, we get: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/0/0e0639a09c7c05f4da3c9848807172495ac7433d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[PD = \\frac{xy}{x+y}\\]\" width=\"98\" height=\"36\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/1/cc1dee5e5a07c277bbde0f08d513bca7e41f75c1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[FP = \\frac{x(x+y)}{y}\\]\" width=\"121\" height=\"42\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/d/70da139b58f4cc0feae3d8d86ddaf5dd76828537.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[EP = \\frac{y(x+y)}{x}\\]\" width=\"120\" height=\"38\" />\nThen\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/c/75ce0a99b696836ec5457438231fcd96de9bf073.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[\\triangle{FDE}] = \\frac{1}{2}\\sin(120)(PDFP + FPEP + EPPD)\\]\" width=\"403\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/f/68fa88afa4775cbc60c6f5c0669ff5d1760df667.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}(x^2 + (x+y)^2 + y^2)\\]\" width=\"202\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/a/fba9d652d50eb82fc81b9b7fb1af18c8b10cf26a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}(x^2 + xy + y^2)\\]\" width=\"158\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/8/9585b61a866a8a7d0697478b21970e0023a2f16e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} BC^2\\]\" width=\"81\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/6/226c79a7b05c4564bb6fdd2ce9cfb3346f0c3d18.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= 2 [\\triangle{ABC}]\\]\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>By Mathdummy.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAJMO\" title=\"2017 USAJMO\">2017 USAJMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAJMO_Problems\" title=\"2017 USAJMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=176&amp;year=2017\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2017 USAJMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2017 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2017 USAJMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2017 USAJMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2017 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2017 USAJMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2017 USAJMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAJMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAJMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAJMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018004120\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.069 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.727 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 867/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 991/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 48/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 32162/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   11.849      1 Template:USAJMO_newbox\n100.00%   11.849      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:15558:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018004120 and revision id 288235. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}